+## 16. SOURCE/TEST implementation-review checkpoint
+
+Selected Contents now resolves the active inventory revision and exact occurrence IDs.
+The identity plan presents each target, source blocker, conditional provider selector,
+request attribution, reuse, shared retries and expiration. Discovery requires confirmation.
+Durable status recovers requests and original evidence dates on reload. Individual review
+admits a supported binding or records rejection. Once mapped, the selected rows can open
+the existing price planner and its separate confirmation.
+
+Migration `0021_selected_component_mapping` adds a mapping operation scope, request
+graph, target edges, bounded typed evidence and durable review receipts. The existing
+provider attempt ledger counts dispatch and retries. PostgreSQL enforces source and
+policy compatibility, current deadlines, lease ownership, both mapping uniqueness
+checks and transactional admission. Runtime has read access to mappings and reviews
+and narrowly granted capabilities. A downgrade across retained mapping history fails.
+Purge removes expired provider payloads and preserves authorized mapping lineage.
+
+Synthetic PostgreSQL and browser evidence includes an additional printed variant
+bound to BrickLink fixture color 17 after four identity requests. The unsupported
+figure stayed blocked. A separate fixture established the uniquely mapped-parent
+whole-figure path. Mixed, ambiguous and conflicting evidence exposed individual
+blockers. Two colors sharing a converged part required six initials. Seven and eight
+initials were refused. A second set joined the original work at zero cost, and a new
+plan reused eligible evidence with its original dates. Desktop and narrow Chromium
+exercised reload, individual approval and a separately confirmable Used/Sold price
+request. Mapping activity produced zero price requests.
